      "author_id": 1,
      "title": "Discussion: CAP Theorem Trade-offs in Real-World Systems",
      "content": "When designing systems like Amazon DynamoDB or Apache Cassandra, how do practical engineering teams balance between Consistency and Availability during unexpected cross-datacenter cable cuts? Share your thoughts below!",
      "is_pinned": 1,
      "is_locked": 0,
      "created_at": "2026-09-10 10:00:00"
    }
  ],
  "forum_replies": [
    {
      "id": 14,
      "topic_id": 1,
      "author_id": 2,
      "content": "Dynamo chooses high availability for shopping cart writes (using vector clocks and client-side reconciliation) because dropping a user checkout order costs real revenue.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-10 14:32:00"
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "topic_id": 1,
      "author_id": 5,
      "content": "In contrast, financial ledger databases and distributed lock managers like Chubby or etcd strictly prioritize Consistency—returning an error or waiting on leader election rather than serving stale state.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-10 15:45:00"
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "topic_id": 1,
      "author_id": 2,
      "content": "Testing distributed consensus with automated verification runner.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-19 04:29:38"
    }
  ],
